    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Lb6zLUaPEBFvya5izBqrtg)_\n\n**Stacked on #193** (base branch `193-author-notes`; retarget to `main` once #193 is merged).\n\nAdds `sp-author-notes-bibtex` (`M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex`): the \"additional\" view of the author notes, for works that exist only as BibTeX entries.\n\n- Reads the `.bib` files of `sp-bibtex-files` (keys like `smith2020attention`).\n- Compares the title of every `:person:` note with each entry's `author` field: **exact** after flipping `Last, First`, **possible** when last name and first initial agree.\n- Leaves out entries that already have a litnote (key found in the head or file name of a note in `litnotes/`: `REFERENCES`, `ROAM_REFS`, `#+reference:`, `@key`).\n- Report buffer, one section per author note. `c` creates the litnote for the entry at point, `C` for all exact entries of the section (both ask first), `RET`/`o` visit, `g` refreshes.\n- The note is made by `sp-author-notes-bibtex-create-function` (`citar-create-note` by default, so the `sp-litnotes` templates apply), then a `- pub-author :: [[id:...][Name]]` line is added so it joins the `Works` table.\n\nDocs: `docs/tangles/funct/sp-author-notes-bibtex.org` (the `.el` is tangled from it), README and CHANGELOG entries, loaded in `init.el` after `sp-author-notes`.\n\n## Tested\n4 ERT tests (`tests/sp-author-notes-bibtex-test.el`) in Emacs 29.3 batch with a temporary vault and the note creation stubbed: name matching, uncovered entries per author, create-and-link, report buffer. The 8 tests of #193 still pass.\n\n## Not tested\nThe real vault and `.bib` files, `citar-create-note` with `citar-denote`/`citar-vulpea`, the report buffer in a GUI.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCGKADQAoj3Npy31mx)_",
